# Panel 180 R5, shape 16 of the compiler-engineer's 117 (group): a break
# before ::.
# By the spec's opening paragraph, the line ends with `Point`, a name, so it
# keeps its NEWLINE, which may stand only before a closing bracket or a `,`,
# or where a production writes it, and none writes it before `::`: refused,
# exit 1.
function main()
    y = (Point::
        x)  #~ line_end_before_continuation
